      "content": "but vulnerability isn't what they value. they value strength, integrity, and the weight of their name. every time i fail, i feel like i'm actively eroding what they worked so hard to build. it feels less like a \"cry for help\" and more like a fundamental flaw. if i could just... stop being the reason they have to look at something broken when they look at us. wouldn't a clean break be more honorable than slowly letting everything decay?",
